{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510424-would-this-power-be-considered-overpowered","id":1510424,"title":"Would this power be considered overpowered?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-01T15:31:15-07:00","id":1510424,"title":"Would this power be considered overpowered?","content":"I used Chat GPT to write up this path because I was quite a fan of Update, one of the aliens within the Omnitrix from the cartoon Ben 10, and wanted to see what a path based on him would look like. Safe to say, I wasn't dissaponted. Might go against the themes of VTM, probably needs some tweaking, and perhaps a bit unbalanced.<br /> <br /> This is a link to Upgrades's wiki page if anyones interested. <a href=\"https://ben10.fandom.com/wiki/Upgrade_(Classic\" target=\"_blank\">https://ben10.fandom.com/wiki/Upgrade_(Classic</a>)<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts?\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> Me- Path for VTm but based off Upgrade from Ben 10<br /> <br /> ChatGPT<br /> <br /> Path Name: Metamorphic Integration<br /> <br /> Overview: Metamorphic Integration is a unique path of Blood Magic inspired by the transformative abilities of Upgrade from Ben 10. It allows vampires to merge with and assimilate technology, objects, and even other creatures into their own bodies, granting them new abilities and powers.<br /> <br /> 1. Morphogenic Adaptation: The vampire can modify their body's shape and structure to adapt to different situations. This ability enables them to reshape their limbs, alter their physical appearance, or even transform parts of their body into various tools or weapons. They can generate extra limbs, elongate their limbs to reach distant objects, or change their form to mimic other creatures.<br /> <br /> 2. Techno-Assimilation: The vampire gains the ability to merge with and assimilate technology, allowing them to incorporate mechanical devices and gadgets directly into their own body. By touching an object or a piece of technology, the vampire can fuse it with their own flesh, gaining the ability to use its functions and abilities. For example, they can integrate a weapon to gain ranged combat capabilities or absorb a computer to access and manipulate digital information.<br /> <br /> 3. Assimilative Absorption: The vampire gains the power to assimilate other creatures into their own body, temporarily absorbing their attributes and abilities. By making physical contact with a target, the vampire can absorb their physical characteristics, skills, and even supernatural powers. This ability allows the vampire to selectively borrow the traits of others, providing them with enhanced combat abilities, supernatural powers, or specialized knowledge.<br /> <br /> 4. Technomantic Interface: The vampire can mentally interface with machines and technological systems, gaining control over them through their blood connection. By touching a device or accessing a network, the vampire can manipulate and override its functions, hack into secure systems, or even disrupt technological infrastructure. This ability allows the vampire to control and manipulate technology with their mind, utilizing it to their advantage.<br /> <br /> 5. Hyper-Evolution: The vampire's assimilation abilities reach their peak, granting them the power of rapid evolution. By merging with multiple objects or creatures simultaneously, the vampire can undergo a temporary metamorphosis, combining and enhancing the abilities they have assimilated. This grants them extraordinary powers and versatility, making them a formidable force on the battlefield. However, this transformation is temporary and requires a substantial amount of blood to initiate.<br /> <br /> Note: As with any homebrew adaptation, it's crucial to discuss and collaborate with the Storyteller to balance the mechanics and ensure that the abilities are in line with the Vampire: The Masquerade setting. The power level, limitations, and thematic integration should be carefully adjusted to fit the game's narrative and maintain game balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Me- Can you give some mechanics?<br /> <br /> ChatGPT<br /> <br /> Certainly! Here are some mechanics you can use to implement the abilities of the Metamorphic Integration path for Vampire: The Masquerade, inspired by Upgrade from Ben 10:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Morphogenic Adaptation:<ul><li>Spend a Blood Point and make a Manipulation + Shapechanging roll to reshape your body or manifest additional limbs.</li> <li>The number of successes determines the extent and precision of the morphological changes you can achieve.</li> <li>The Storyteller determines the limitations and possibilities of each transformation, keeping in mind the character's Blood Potency and Clan/Bloodline disciplines.</li> </ul></li> <li>Techno-Assimilation:<ul><li>Spend a Blood Point and make a Dexterity + Technology roll to successfully assimilate a technological object into your body.</li> <li>The number of successes determines the level of integration and the complexity of the device you can assimilate.</li> <li>Once assimilated, you gain access to the functions and abilities of the integrated technology. The Storyteller determines the specific benefits based on the assimilated object.</li> </ul></li> <li>Assimilative Absorption:<ul><li>Spend a Blood Point and make a Strength + Blood Magic roll to successfully absorb the traits of another creature.</li> <li>The number of successes determines the duration and potency of the absorbed traits.</li> <li>The Storyteller determines the specific benefits based on the absorbed creature, considering their traits, skills, and supernatural abilities.</li> </ul></li> <li>Technomantic Interface:<ul><li>Spend a Blood Point and make an Intelligence + Computer roll to interface with a technological device or network.</li> <li>The number of successes determines the level of control you can exert over the technology.</li> <li>The Storyteller determines the specific actions and limitations of your manipulation, considering the complexity of the technology involved.</li> </ul></li> <li>Hyper-Evolution:<ul><li>Spend a significant amount of Blood Points (determined by the Storyteller) and make a Resolve + Blood Magic roll to trigger hyper-evolution.</li> <li>The number of successes determines the duration and the scope of the metamorphosis.</li> <li>The Storyteller determines the specific enhancements and abilities gained during the hyper-evolved state, taking into account the character's assimilated traits and the narrative context.</li> </ul></li> </ol><br /> Remember, these mechanics are meant to provide a starting point, and it's essential to work with your Storyteller to fine-tune and adapt them to your specific Vampire: The Masquerade campaign.<br /> \u200b<br /> *(Morphogenic Adaption &amp; Techno Assimilation were levels 2 and 1 respectively, but I felt the power progression didnt make sense, so I switched their places)-Me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-01-2023, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}